Subject: [PATCH] sprint 9: self-serve subscription checkout for coaching
 programs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds an end-to-end Stripe Checkout flow so parents can enroll in
Foundation / Acceleration / Elite coaching directly from the pricing
page or diagnostic results — no consultation required.

Flow:
- /enroll/[tier] confirmation page: program summary, features,
  three trust badges (cancel anytime / micro-cohort / secure),
  optional email prefill, big 'Continue to Checkout' button.
- Server action createSubscriptionCheckout builds a Stripe hosted
  Checkout session in mode:'subscription' with two custom fields
  (student name, student grade), promo codes enabled, address
  collection required.
- Webhook /api/stripe/subscription-webhook handles
  checkout.session.completed and the customer.subscription.*
  lifecycle. On completion it upserts to program_subscriptions
  and emails the parent a Supabase magic-link welcome so they
  can set up their account in one click.
- /enroll/success shows a personalized thank-you with a 3-step
  'what happens next' timeline. /enroll/cancel handles abandons
  gracefully.
- Pricing 'Enroll Now' buttons and diagnostic-results 'Enroll in
  [Program]' button now route to /enroll/[tier].

Infrastructure:
- New migration 00049_program_subscriptions.sql: family_id +
  stripe_customer_id/subscription_id/status/period, RLS for
  parents + admins, updated_at trigger.
- New lib/stripe/programs.ts holds tier config + env-var price
  ID lookup so switching between test/live only touches env vars.
- Middleware allows /enroll publicly (checkout must work for
  anonymous visitors).
- docs/stripe-subscription-setup.md: step-by-step Stripe product
  creation, env-var checklist, webhook config, smoke-test, and
  go-live instructions.

Env vars required (all three environments):
  STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET,
  STRIPE_PRICE_ID_FOUNDATION, STRIPE_PRICE_ID_ACCELERATION,
  STRIPE_PRICE_ID_ELITE
